# apps/web's build settings for prod, which `make -C infra web-build` reads before `bun run build`
# (dl-e8ov.2.64). Nothing here is secret: the browser holds all of it. This file wins over your
# shell, so a build has exactly what is written here, and an empty value means none.
#
# Prod sign-in is on and linked from jadwigo.pl/zaloguj (decision dl-asgl): the email code, Google,
# and Facebook for the Meta app's testers. The lawyer-reviewed consent text (dl-e8ov.2.9) no longer
# gates it.
# JW_SUPABASE_URL is jadwigo-prod's supabase.co host for now (decision dl-2qke). Once the custom
# domain is active (dl-e8ov.2.75) it becomes https://auth.jadwigo.pl, followed by a web redeploy.
# JW_SUPABASE_KEY is jadwigo-prod's publishable key (sb_publishable_…), never a secret key. Its
# line carries gitleaks:allow because the browser holds it by design.
# JW_SUPABASE_PROVIDERS is a comma list of the buttons shown: google, facebook. Facebook stays off
# the list while the Meta app is in Development mode (decision dl-ovva): the project has it on, and
# testers start it with app.jadwigo.pl/parent?provider=facebook. Once the app is Live it becomes
# google,facebook.
JW_SUPABASE_URL=https://xhzkmpainwzrfktxffjv.supabase.co
JW_SUPABASE_KEY=sb_publishable_4Xjr1KlY2CRbn8L5OO6cHQ_mRCyjznO # gitleaks:allow
JW_SUPABASE_PROVIDERS=google

# Where the app loads a question's pictures: the media CloudFront over the content bucket's
# khan/media/ (dl-n9fr.52, dl-n9fr.53). It is terraform's `media_url` output and the SSM parameter
# /jadwigo/bank/media-url. Left empty, a picture ref stays a same-origin path and does not load.
VITE_MEDIA_URL=https://dx5i3bka3zn5f.cloudfront.net
